{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>If</b> — the words of each of the poets are in their heart." "And the sense of <b>if I forget you</b> — corresponding to <b>when we remembered</b>." "And the sense of <b>my right hand</b> — on account of our lyres, for with the right hand is the plucking of strings and playing." "<b>May my right hand forget</b> — it is missing [an object], like המעשה, and he said of the right hand: תשכח, by way of parable." "And some say: its meaning is: <b>may it wither</b> — without a companion [i.e., without כה]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 137, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:41:57.751990673Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}